we can detect planets outside our solar  system by the gravitational effects that  these planets have on their stars small  planets like Earth weigh much less than  their star when those planets move in  their orbits the effect on the star is  very hard to see the force they exert on  each other is comparatively small so the  star barely moves as the planet orbits  around it large planets like Jupiter  have a greater gravitational influence  on their star but when the planets are  far away the effect is still fairly  small the planet and star are orbiting a  common center point but it's close to  the center of the star however we found  planets that are larger than Jupiter and  which orbit much closer to their star  than Jupiter is to our Sun the effect of  gravity is much stronger in these cases  with such large planets it's easier to  see that the planets gravity affects the  Stars motion and that the two orbit a  common center we can't see the star move  back and forth because the stars are  very very very very far away from us  instead we use the Doppler effect the  same effect that causes sound to change  pitch when its source moves when a  source of waves moves towards us we hear  it as higher-pitched when the wave  source moves away from us we hear a  lower pitch in terms of light frequency  that corresponds to light moving more  towards blue higher frequency or more  towards red lower frequency the effect  is small so we don't see it in our  day-to-day lives but we can detect it  with a spectrometer as the exoplanet  moves away from us the star comes  towards us so the light becomes ever so  slightly more blue on the other side of  the orbit as the star moves away from us  the light from the star becomes slightly  more red  the amount of shift the difference from  blue to red light tells us how fast the  star is moving that in turn tells us  whether we have a light planet a medium  planet or a heavy planet affecting the  movement of the star and that's the  wobble method that's true that's one  thing we don't have right in this is  it's not spinning okay are you ready  you
 

